ser}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-26T22:33:59Z","updated_at":"2024-11-26T22:33:59Z","body":"**Problem**: The child tablet (from a split) has incorrect metadata - min_schema_version is 2, while some of the rows in the SST files corresponding to the tablet are on schema_version 0. This is a persistent corruption on that tablet and it cannot be fixed. The tablet needs to be removed from the cluster, and RBSed from a healthy peer (if one exists).\r\n\r\n**Conditions**: It seems like the parent of the split went through a compaction and decided to update its own min_schema_version  to 2, even though it was in the middle of a split. It is unclear why the child tablet has  incorrect metadata - min_schema_version  of 2. \r\n\r\n@Huqicheng to continue to inspect code and possibly try to repro the scenario in an unit test environment","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/2502070273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rthallamko3","id":17170123,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTcwMTIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17170123?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthallamko3","html_url":"https://github.com/rthallamko3","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rthall